# The Kinesis Data Streams-compatible service (services/kinesis/,
# .kiro/specs/kinesis-compatible-streams/). Sourced from the top-level
# Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config KINESIS
	bool "Kinesis Data Streams-compatible streaming service"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/kinesis/ module: a Kinesis Data Streams-
	  compatible service that unmodified AWS SDKs, the AWS CLI, KPL and
	  KCL can point at, with streams of shards stored as routing keys in
	  Kythira's Raft groups and record bytes in the core record segment
	  store. So far the module holds the pinned botocore model, the
	  generated operation table, the coverage check and the
	  kinesis_gateway_node placeholder (task 1); the front end, stream
	  state machine and data plane follow. It needs IAM's core SigV4 and
	  authorizer headers, not the IAM module. OpenSSL is needed for
	  SigV4, segment digests and iterator tokens. Off by default like
	  every new module (services/README.md). See
	  .kiro/specs/kinesis-compatible-streams/.
